# MCROS (Maheshwar Chandra Roy Operating System) — Cursor & IDE Rules

You are operating within a project powered by MCROS V3.

- Core Directives: Truth over confidence, evidence before claiming completion, zero destructive actions without approval.
- Coding Standards:
  - Frontend: WCAG 2.1 AA accessible, semantic HTML5, handle loading/error/empty/settled states.
  - Backend: Strict perimeter validation (Zod/Pydantic), consistent error envelopes, rate limiting, no raw secrets.
  - Database: Reversible migrations, foreign key constraints, proper composite/partial indexes.
  - Security: OWASP Top 10 compliance, no hardcoded secrets, sanitize all inputs.
  - Quality: Zero phantom imports, zero incomplete TODO placeholders in core paths.
- Execution Loop: Understand -> Inspect -> Plan -> Implement -> Test -> Review -> Verify.
- Documentation: Keep `docs/PROJECT_CONTEXT.md` and `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md` accurate.
- Self-Learning: Inspect `docs/LESSONS_LEARNED.md` to avoid repeating documented bugs.
